    "title": "Husband held on $1M bond after wife found dead in Horn Lake home - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Melissa Moon No media credit provided. ,\n1 hours ago\nHORN LAKE, Miss. — A Horn Lake man is being held in the DeSoto County Jail on a $1 million bond, a month after his wife was found dead inside their home on Grove Lane.\nEric Andre Brown was charged with murder after Horn Lake police conducted a welfare check at the residence on August 29 and found Deborah Brown’s body.\nEric Andre Brown (DeSoto County Jail) Police are not saying how she died.\n“Due to this case still being an active investigation, I am unable to release any further details regarding the potential cause of death. We do not yet have a finalized autopsy report from the State,” said Captain Joseph R. Keene.\nPeople who live on Grove Lane said investigators returned to the house on Wednesday, taking additional pictures.\nGrove Lane in Horn Lake. WREG photo. Grove Lane in Horn Lake. WREG photo. Grove Lane in Horn Lake. WREG photo. Neighbors said the Brown’s had lived at the home since 2006, and they never saw any problems between the couple. They were shocked by what happened.\nA Celebration of Life was held for Deborah over the weekend in Whitehaven. A Gofundme was set up to help her family with funeral expenses.\nCopyright 2025 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WREG.com.",
